{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The smallest.</b> The smallest family, whose number is few, shall become a thousand." "<b>In its time.</b> At the appointed time of salvation. The correct reading is that it is joined with \"the smallest shall become a thousand,\" and behold, I will hasten to make them, while still young, into a mighty nation, in the manner of \"and I will make you into a great nation\" (Genesis 12:2)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:33.638544480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}